From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saphira forward-port <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
Date: Thu, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [FWD 7.2.9] mm: refactor find_next_best_node to
 find_next_best_node_in

Fwd-port of upstream 0b62c90ff822 ("mm: refactor find_next_best_node
to find_next_best_node_in", Gregory Price, 2026-06-16, series position
014) onto Linux 7.2.9.

Why needed: between the branch base (Jul-20 master) and 7.2.9, upstream
changed the node_reclaim() declaration in mm/internal.h (unsigned long +
named params -> int + anonymous params; the !CONFIG_NUMA stub now
returns NODE_RECLAIM_NOSCAN). Only the two mm/internal.h hunks needed
context refresh; memory-tiers.c and page_alloc.c hunks are verbatim
upstream. Final diffstat identical to upstream (16+/10- across the same
3 files).

Byte-identical upstream patch retained in series/ (recorded SKIP-FWD).
Verifies with git apply --check (no fuzz).

Signed-off-by: Saphira builder <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
---
diff --git a/mm/internal.h b/mm/internal.h
index 08ecc61..8e56c0a 100644
--- a/mm/internal.h
+++ b/mm/internal.h
@@ -1390,7 +1390,8 @@ static inline void mminit_verify_zonelist(void)
 extern int node_reclaim_mode;
 
 extern int node_reclaim(struct pglist_data *, gfp_t, unsigned int);
-extern int find_next_best_node(int node, nodemask_t *used_node_mask);
+extern int find_next_best_node_in(int node, nodemask_t *used_node_mask,
+				  const nodemask_t *candidates);
 #else
 #define node_reclaim_mode 0
 
@@ -1399,7 +1400,8 @@ static inline int node_reclaim(struct pglist_data *pgdat, gfp_t mask,
 {
 	return NODE_RECLAIM_NOSCAN;
 }
-static inline int find_next_best_node(int node, nodemask_t *used_node_mask)
+static inline int find_next_best_node_in(int node, nodemask_t *used_node_mask,
+					 const nodemask_t *candidates)
 {
 	return NUMA_NO_NODE;
 }
